WEBVTT

00:10.530 --> 00:16.000
Since ancient times, the Gods of the Dragon
and the Gods of Evil have fought.

00:16.400 --> 00:21.750
The Gods of Evil have the power to
destroy humanity in an instant.

00:22.130 --> 00:28.220
But that power was sealed by those whose
veins hold the blood of the Dragon Gods.

02:05.130 --> 02:10.630
Ninja Ryukenden
(Ninja Gaiden)

04:09.460 --> 04:10.450
Ryu!

04:10.430 --> 04:11.530
You're still here?

04:12.140 --> 04:13.890
You didn't need to stay here, you know.

04:14.500 --> 04:15.880
Did something happen?

04:19.380 --> 04:22.120
Oh, that's... Are you hurt?

04:23.250 --> 04:24.620
It's nothing.

04:26.380 --> 04:29.860
You're still good for my birthday, right?

04:31.180 --> 04:33.280
I've already got the restaurant reserved!

04:33.780 --> 04:36.750
Sorry.... It's just a bad time.

04:37.790 --> 04:39.740
But you promised me a long time ago.

04:41.450 --> 04:44.030
I'm sorry. I'll make it up to you next tme. {TL Check}

04:44.030 --> 04:46.900
But you promised...

05:17.560 --> 05:22.460
I don't really understand
how Ryu feels about me...

05:22.490 --> 05:27.650
Don't get so down over a missed
birthday dinner, Irene.

05:27.700 --> 05:28.890
But...

05:29.310 --> 05:31.440
Come on, don't make that face.

05:31.790 --> 05:34.460
Just think of something else!

05:34.460 --> 05:38.460
But, I'm not really good at that...

05:38.630 --> 05:40.880
I'm saying that's the problem with you.

05:40.970 --> 05:43.280
You're serious about Ryu, aren't you?

05:44.560 --> 05:48.780
Then you can't just keep waiting! 
You need to snatch him up.

05:53.940 --> 05:56.950
If you're that worried, I'll make sure of it for you.

06:00.440 --> 06:03.030
I'll ask Robert to ask him how he feels about you.

06:05.280 --> 06:06.960
Okay then, I'll see you later.

06:25.100 --> 06:28.390
Stay out of their problems!

06:28.440 --> 06:30.470
It's not something for us to meddle with.

06:30.570 --> 06:35.110
But at this rate, those two'll grow old 
before they even hold hands!

06:35.110 --> 06:37.150
You're just being nosy.

06:37.150 --> 06:39.780
You always stick your nose
in where it doesn't belong.

06:39.780 --> 06:46.320
My... Who was it that said they liked
my strong curiosity, Mr. Detective?

06:49.030 --> 06:51.900
Now that I think about it, I've
heard that too, Robert.

06:51.900 --> 06:52.830
Right, Jeff?

06:54.460 --> 06:58.580
I just need you to ask him how he
feels, okay? You're friends, right?

06:59.670 --> 07:01.360
I knew you'd be here!

07:01.360 --> 07:02.100
Hi!

07:02.260 --> 07:05.880
Sara, the Chief's calling for you. He says
he needs you to cover something.

07:07.060 --> 07:08.040
Is this right?

07:08.400 --> 07:10.250
Huh? What's this now?

07:11.800 --> 07:15.580
The genius bio-technologist and
CEO of the Friedman Corporation,

07:15.580 --> 07:20.290
Ned Friedman, announces a cure
for cancer with no side effects!

07:20.300 --> 07:22.370
It'll be a joint press conference, most likely.

07:22.630 --> 07:24.860
I don't feel like writing the same
article as everybody else.

07:25.360 --> 07:27.960
It'd just end up being useless.

07:28.500 --> 07:30.870
Then, what should I say to the Chief?

07:33.870 --> 07:37.040
I know. I'll ask for a private interview!

07:37.410 --> 07:39.980
In that case, I'll have to get some things ready.

07:40.680 --> 07:43.490
See you, Robert! Take care of Irene for me.

07:43.490 --> 07:44.720
H-Hey!

07:47.400 --> 07:50.280
You're weak when it comes
to the girl you love, huh?

07:54.220 --> 07:57.090
- Be sure to take good photos!
- Just leave the work to me!

07:57.790 --> 07:59.100
I'll get the scoop!

07:59.900 --> 08:01.350
He sure is late, though.

08:01.350 --> 08:03.030
What's he doing?

08:03.530 --> 08:05.470
If it's true, it'll be such huge news!

08:06.740 --> 08:07.870
Scoop! Scoop!

08:08.640 --> 08:09.470
Come on already!

08:09.940 --> 08:12.710
- Oh! It's opening, it's opening!
- Let's go!

08:13.610 --> 08:14.410
Scoop!

08:19.120 --> 08:20.450
- Professor Friedman!
- Professor!

08:20.450 --> 08:21.950
Please give us any comments you have!

08:22.620 --> 08:24.460
Is your cure for cancer real?

08:25.090 --> 08:27.630
- Are there really no side effects? 
- Is it safe to use?

08:29.130 --> 08:32.060
- Professor Friedman! 
- Professor, don't just sit there, say something, please!

08:32.600 --> 08:33.900
- Professor!
- Professor Friedman!

08:34.460 --> 08:36.060
The medicine, does it really work?

08:36.060 --> 08:37.470
Is it true?

08:45.880 --> 08:47.080
<i>Save me!</i>

08:49.250 --> 08:53.320
<i>Somebody... Somebody, save me! Please!</i>

08:56.250 --> 08:58.390
<i>Let me out of here!</i>

09:16.070 --> 09:17.070
Tails...

09:17.420 --> 09:19.100
Tails, huh?

09:23.450 --> 09:25.180
Am I gonna be paying
 for the rest of my life?

09:25.180 --> 09:26.680
My bad...

09:26.680 --> 09:30.220
Another round! It's on Robert again tonight.

09:32.220 --> 09:33.190
Sorry to keep you waiting!

09:33.290 --> 09:33.890
Yo!

09:35.350 --> 09:36.660
I'll take my usual.

09:37.630 --> 09:42.580
- I haven't asked Ryu yet...
- Forget about that. I've found something interesting.

09:42.580 --> 09:44.500
About Ned Friedman.

09:44.500 --> 09:46.570
You interviewed him, didn't you?

09:46.570 --> 09:52.270
I got turned down. And I heard that even at the 
joint press conference, he didn't say a word.

09:52.980 --> 09:54.920
This is Ned Friedman we're talking about here!

09:54.920 --> 09:57.830
He loves the media, and he's always 
bragging about his latest achievements.

09:57.830 --> 09:59.460
Don't you think something's up?

09:59.720 --> 10:03.290
And there's another crazy rumor about him.

10:03.870 --> 10:05.370
What is it?

10:05.390 --> 10:07.720
So, think you could help me for a little?

10:13.140 --> 10:15.180
What's the rumor?

10:15.200 --> 10:16.520
Human Experiments.

10:16.860 --> 10:17.980
You're kidding me.

10:18.570 --> 10:23.160
Strange screams are heard from his house, and once
 in a while, large boxes are carried out of it.

10:23.670 --> 10:25.240
It's just a neighborhood rumor, though.

10:25.380 --> 10:27.780
Jeez, we're going to a place like that?

10:27.780 --> 10:29.210
Yup! Of course we are!

11:05.380 --> 11:06.650
Can we get in?

11:06.650 --> 11:08.570
No, it's locked.

11:11.860 --> 11:13.460
H-Hey!

11:13.590 --> 11:15.530
Why did it open?

11:23.880 --> 11:25.410
Wonder if anybody's home.

11:25.940 --> 11:29.420
See, see? It's just like I said. Let's go home.

11:29.770 --> 11:33.320
I'm sure the genius professor
is sleeping at his company.

11:33.390 --> 11:35.780
And the rumors were just rumors, okay?

11:35.830 --> 11:37.380
Right, Robert?

11:41.410 --> 11:44.790
This place is a mess... Who did this?

11:51.390 --> 11:55.200
Do you think the screams were from
Ned? He was killed a long while ago.

11:55.200 --> 11:59.390
Wait, then who was the Ned Friedman
 that developed the cure for cancer?

11:59.920 --> 12:02.550
He didn't even say a word
at that press conference, right?

12:03.040 --> 12:04.930
So maybe it was a double?

12:05.200 --> 12:06.770
No way.

12:06.860 --> 12:07.680
Let's split up.

12:09.680 --> 12:12.720
Listen, Jeff, make sure to check things
 out thoroughly. This is work, after all.

12:13.580 --> 12:16.180
Did anyone actually hear those screams?

12:16.220 --> 12:19.700
It'd be bad if those were the
screams of Ned's ghost!

12:19.730 --> 12:21.970
Then shall we call the Ghostbusters?

12:22.530 --> 12:24.700
That's not funny.

12:33.440 --> 12:35.760
Hey, they're connected.

13:05.310 --> 13:06.430
Sara, stay back!

13:06.640 --> 13:07.510
Robert!

13:09.720 --> 13:10.760
Ryu, huh?

13:13.100 --> 13:13.600
Ryu!

13:20.070 --> 13:21.730
What's with that outfit?

13:21.940 --> 13:23.900
Robert, what are you doing here?

13:23.900 --> 13:25.610
Helping Sara out.

13:25.780 --> 13:28.590
It seems there are strange
rumors involving Ned Friedman.

13:30.460 --> 13:31.090
Rumors?

13:31.510 --> 13:35.090
They say he's been doing human 
experiments... Biotechnological ones.

13:35.890 --> 13:37.430
Biotechnology?

13:43.850 --> 13:44.670
Jeff!

13:49.690 --> 13:50.730
Where are you, Jeff?

13:51.070 --> 13:52.030
Jeff!

13:52.820 --> 13:53.770
Over there!

13:59.290 --> 14:00.620
Jeff, are you okay?

14:03.620 --> 14:04.810
Ryu...

14:05.580 --> 14:06.590
Robert...

14:08.130 --> 14:08.860
Jeff!

14:09.250 --> 14:10.960
L-Look at that!

14:21.390 --> 14:22.800
They're dead, aren't they?

14:22.800 --> 14:23.890
Looks like it.

14:27.440 --> 14:28.600
Sara, get your camera.

14:35.740 --> 14:37.560
The rumors were true.

14:38.110 --> 14:39.490
Human experiments.

14:40.030 --> 14:43.800
I heard once that the Friedman Corporation
was doing research on biological weapons...

14:44.160 --> 14:45.660
That would be this, huh?

14:45.710 --> 14:47.820
Why would they make something like this?

14:47.830 --> 14:49.760
Are they nuts?

14:49.960 --> 14:51.040
You're too loud!

14:51.090 --> 14:52.010
Calm down, Jeff!

14:52.010 --> 14:53.340
I am calm.

14:53.340 --> 14:54.500
Anyway, this is a scoop.

14:56.710 --> 14:57.510
Hey!

14:59.550 --> 15:00.820
What are you doing?

15:00.830 --> 15:03.320
I'm sorry, but I'd rather you didn't
make an article out of this.

15:03.770 --> 15:05.420
You've got to be kidding me!

15:05.420 --> 15:08.100
Why should I have to take that
 kind of order from you, Ryu?!

15:12.110 --> 15:14.020
It'd be better if you didn't get involved.

15:14.070 --> 15:15.070
Why?

15:15.820 --> 15:18.890
- It's better not to know.
- Don't tell me how to do my job!

15:19.360 --> 15:21.490
Just don't make an article out of it, please.

15:21.810 --> 15:23.990
I've finally gotten a scoop, though!

15:28.460 --> 15:30.750
Are you going to try and
hide things from me, too?

15:30.990 --> 15:31.750
Out with it.

15:31.900 --> 15:34.800
Somebody's trying to break the seal
of the Evil God, aren't they?

15:35.220 --> 15:38.040
And that somebody's Ned Friedman, isn't it?

15:40.780 --> 15:43.930
If you can't say, that means that I
can assume I'm right, huh?

15:46.390 --> 15:52.100
We'd finally beaten that Jaquio, too. 
Everybody wants the power of the Evil God!

15:54.470 --> 15:56.910
It was back when I was in
the Army Special Forces.

16:00.660 --> 16:06.410
A guy named Jaquio was trying to break the seal on the Evil God, so I was ordered to stop him.

16:07.060 --> 16:10.130
I didn't really believe in the Evil God.

16:11.530 --> 16:15.070
Then you, the Dragon Ninja, appeared.

16:17.470 --> 16:22.570
I quit the army because I intended to fight alongside you, when somebody else

16:22.800 --> 16:24.890
who tried to call forth the Evil God appeared!

16:34.020 --> 16:34.900
Ryu!

16:35.210 --> 16:36.920
Can you still not tell me?!

16:46.620 --> 16:48.040
Please understand, Robert.

16:49.110 --> 16:53.330
This is my destiny as the Dragon Ninja.

16:53.820 --> 16:55.030
I don't want to let anybody die.

16:55.390 --> 16:57.190
Not you, not Sara, and not Jeffrey.

16:57.980 --> 16:58.890
Or Irene!

17:00.920 --> 17:01.770
Ryu!

17:08.240 --> 17:12.740
Professor Bucky-Wise, let's get right to the point. I'd like to ask you about Ned Friedman.

17:13.730 --> 17:18.270
You know, I haven't seen Ned
 Friedman since we were students...

17:18.470 --> 17:23.260
That was almost 20 years ago, and we
were never that close to begin with.

17:23.490 --> 17:30.240
Even back then, he decided that he was a genius, and he wouldn't speak to the likes of me.

17:31.210 --> 17:34.100
By the way, would you like another cup of coffee?

17:34.540 --> 17:35.750
No, I'm fine.

17:36.530 --> 17:37.830
I see...

17:38.160 --> 17:41.290
I drink coffee too much, I think.

17:42.580 --> 17:44.580
Anyway, what were we talking about?

17:45.130 --> 17:48.000
Oh right, Ned Friedman.

17:48.210 --> 17:51.380
To be honest, he wasn't the type I liked.

17:51.800 --> 17:55.470
I felt at times that he was almost mad.

17:55.890 --> 18:00.890
He always used to say, "I will become the
world's Messiah with my biotechnology."

18:02.350 --> 18:04.270
And what else was there?

18:05.350 --> 18:09.110
He always said he needed some kind of power.

18:09.570 --> 18:11.320
Well, he got it.

18:11.530 --> 18:14.700
If he's conquered cancer, he's
become a kind of Messiah.

18:16.360 --> 18:20.370
Well, you know what they say. There's a
fine line separating genius from insanity.

18:20.540 --> 18:24.190
Though, I think he tilted a little more
towards the "insane" side.

18:24.440 --> 18:25.540
And...

18:25.640 --> 18:29.590
Oh, um, thank you very 
much. You've been a huge help.

18:29.960 --> 18:33.700
You're leaving already? Feel free
to stay longer if you'd like.

18:33.700 --> 18:36.880
It's been a long time since a
woman has come to visit me.

18:37.050 --> 18:38.530
No, this is plenty.

18:39.120 --> 18:40.180
We'll be going.

18:40.330 --> 18:43.440
Come again. Next time, without your bodyguards.

18:44.020 --> 18:47.390
What's with that old man? 
He's just as insane himself.

18:48.850 --> 18:50.240
Some kind of power...

18:51.880 --> 18:53.760
It looks like it's clear who our opponent is.

19:04.580 --> 19:05.960
Thank you.

19:12.760 --> 19:13.790
Did you say something?

19:21.510 --> 19:23.060
Let's close early today.

19:23.060 --> 19:23.600
All right.

19:30.690 --> 19:31.810
- Irene...
- Yes?

19:32.160 --> 19:34.880
You said you had a friend
who lives far away, right?

19:35.490 --> 19:39.560
Yeah, they live in Utah. What about it?

19:42.740 --> 19:43.660
Oh my!

19:44.830 --> 19:46.210
Where did you come from?

19:46.410 --> 19:50.310
Did you get lost? Or are you stray?

20:00.840 --> 20:02.080
What's wrong?

20:06.850 --> 20:08.610
Come on, don't yell.

20:14.320 --> 20:15.840
Irene, hide!

20:31.920 --> 20:32.830
Ryu!

20:37.460 --> 20:38.340
Ryu!

21:11.550 --> 21:12.320
Irene!

21:17.210 --> 21:18.050
Irene!

21:21.240 --> 21:21.980
Irene!

21:24.010 --> 21:24.680
Irene!

21:25.050 --> 21:25.800
Irene!

21:30.820 --> 21:32.640
What are you doing? Go!

21:34.250 --> 21:35.700
Let's go!

21:39.140 --> 21:40.310
They're dead.

22:10.890 --> 22:12.420
Please, stay away from me.

22:13.100 --> 22:15.420
I can't make you happy.

22:18.020 --> 22:18.740
Irene...

22:19.380 --> 22:21.550
I don't want to get you involved in this battle.

22:42.610 --> 22:45.920
I never thought it'd be like this.

22:47.580 --> 22:50.290
I thought we could be together forever.

23:03.280 --> 23:06.700
I'll always be waiting.

23:07.100 --> 23:10.420
For the day you'll come back to me.

23:11.510 --> 23:12.500
I believe in that!

23:21.220 --> 23:22.100
Again?!

23:22.100 --> 23:23.310
Hurry, Robert.

23:23.480 --> 23:25.270
We might catch her at her apartment.

23:25.930 --> 23:26.720
I know that!

23:28.600 --> 23:29.460
Scary.

23:49.580 --> 23:50.450
There she is!

23:53.170 --> 23:53.850
Irene!

23:56.340 --> 23:57.840
Run, Irene!

24:04.850 --> 24:05.550
Get in!

24:16.360 --> 24:18.200
What are those guys?!

24:18.310 --> 24:20.080
There's no time to explain!

24:24.070 --> 24:25.950
Dammit...

24:26.910 --> 24:30.470
If I knew this would happen, I would've bought a Porsche or something!

24:31.000 --> 24:32.380
You couldn't afford one anyway.

24:32.650 --> 24:34.880
Anything faster would've been nice.

24:43.430 --> 24:44.300
You guys okay?

24:45.760 --> 24:47.050
I'm fine.

24:48.100 --> 24:50.180
I'm fine too, somehow!

25:12.530 --> 25:13.640
You moron!

25:19.500 --> 25:21.340
Jeff!

26:32.440 --> 26:35.820
Like I said, I know where they went.

26:39.480 --> 26:41.840
I'll believe what you say.

26:45.180 --> 26:53.160
Ned Friedman kidnapped Irene... to bait Ryu.

27:21.260 --> 27:23.810
Okay, take your favorite.

27:23.810 --> 27:25.520
You know how to use them, don't you?

27:26.610 --> 27:27.600
Jeff...

27:27.600 --> 27:28.910
You can't have...

27:28.920 --> 27:31.000
There's only one thing to do.

27:31.610 --> 27:33.110
Irene's been kidnapped.

27:33.110 --> 27:34.570
We know where she was taken.

27:36.150 --> 27:38.070
I'll take this one.

27:38.270 --> 27:40.430
It's best to take the one you know best.

27:42.300 --> 27:44.160
Jeff, are you going too?

27:44.160 --> 27:45.250
Of course.

27:45.410 --> 27:47.340
Irene is an important friend.

27:52.670 --> 27:53.690
I'm going too.

27:54.550 --> 27:55.940
It's dangerous, Sara.

27:56.530 --> 27:58.340
This is a war.

27:58.420 --> 28:00.430
There's no guarantee you'll come back alive.

28:00.430 --> 28:01.650
You can't stop me.

28:01.710 --> 28:03.680
I can't just leave Irene like that.

28:03.920 --> 28:06.100
Men don't have a monopoly on friendship.

28:06.770 --> 28:08.600
Leave this to us.

28:08.650 --> 28:11.060
For one thing, you can't run in that skirt.

28:21.470 --> 28:23.830
You like my strong curiosity, right?

28:25.320 --> 28:27.540
And that's why I'd rather you stayed alive.

28:28.890 --> 28:31.000
Now then, let's go, partner!

29:00.070 --> 29:02.960
I hope he gets here soon.

29:03.030 --> 29:06.290
I want to see the look on his
face when he sees you.

29:06.310 --> 29:08.210
I'm so looking forward to it.

29:14.670 --> 29:15.210
Jeff!

29:15.210 --> 29:16.140
Robert!

29:16.440 --> 29:17.580
Oh my...

29:17.580 --> 29:21.150
A lot of your friends seem to have a death wish.

29:33.620 --> 29:34.380
Let's go!

29:34.380 --> 29:35.290
Yeah!

29:47.490 --> 29:48.730
Bastard!

30:09.970 --> 30:11.390
Jeff! Are you done yet?

30:11.400 --> 30:12.780
Okay, leave it to me!

30:18.280 --> 30:19.290
Hit it!

30:23.530 --> 30:25.150
Got 'em all.

30:25.160 --> 30:26.360
All right, let's go.

30:28.110 --> 30:29.240
What's wrong, Jeff?

30:29.280 --> 30:30.990
I'm shaking...

30:32.280 --> 30:33.370
Jeff...

30:35.620 --> 30:39.630
My blood longs to fight more than anything.

30:39.690 --> 30:41.380
It's the blood of a demon.

30:42.920 --> 30:44.920
I was a mercenary.

30:44.920 --> 30:48.630
After I quit and went back to the
States, I thought I'd live normally,

30:48.680 --> 30:50.720
so I put on the mask of a coward.

30:50.890 --> 30:53.030
I thought I'd managed to become a coward.

30:53.220 --> 30:56.460
But look at me... I'm happy.

30:56.810 --> 31:00.350
I'm so happy to be back on 
the battlefield that I'm shaking.

31:03.680 --> 31:05.600
Everybody's like that.

31:05.910 --> 31:09.490
We like fighting, we like alcohol,
and we like women.

31:09.610 --> 31:12.120
Some of us even like men.

31:12.370 --> 31:17.930
We all work on the parts that cause trouble,
and somehow get along with the world.

31:18.590 --> 31:20.340
It's not just you.

31:20.340 --> 31:22.630
All right, let's get rid of these
guys and go grab a drink!

31:22.630 --> 31:23.630
Absolutely!

31:25.880 --> 31:27.800
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

31:29.140 --> 31:30.270
<i>Who's there?</i>

31:30.260 --> 31:32.510
<i>Save me, please!</i>

31:32.520 --> 31:33.810
<i>Where are you?</i>

31:34.600 --> 31:36.110
<i>I don't know.</i>

31:36.100 --> 31:38.550
<i>It's dark and cramped in here.</i>

31:38.560 --> 31:40.450
<i>You're inside this building, huh?</i>

31:41.150 --> 31:42.650
<i>Hurry, save me!</i>

31:43.740 --> 31:46.860
<i>Listen, just keep talking to me.</i>

31:46.860 --> 31:49.660
<i>That way, I may be able to find you.</i>

31:51.990 --> 31:53.850
<i>Save me!</i>

31:58.120 --> 32:00.250
Everybody... die.

32:25.860 --> 32:26.550
Hey!

32:26.680 --> 32:28.700
Are these machines to make biological weapons?

32:29.490 --> 32:33.160
T-The President said that they're there
to make a superhuman race.

32:33.180 --> 32:34.080
Superhuman?

32:34.330 --> 32:35.450
Those monsters?

32:36.080 --> 32:37.470
Don't screw with me!

32:38.550 --> 32:40.220
How does it work?

32:40.590 --> 32:42.210
O-Over there.

32:42.680 --> 32:51.270
The genes of the first and second experimental 
subjects are added to human DNA...

32:51.270 --> 32:52.350
Anyway, this is it, right?

32:52.650 --> 32:53.220
Okay, go.

32:53.900 --> 32:54.730
Go now!

33:03.950 --> 33:04.570
Ryu!

33:17.960 --> 33:19.510
Damn you, Dragon Ninja!

33:19.590 --> 33:22.910
After all the work I put into making a
superhuman manufacturing device!

33:22.930 --> 33:26.300
Doesn't he understand human evolution?

33:27.010 --> 33:29.890
Well, no matter. I can make
 as many devices as I'd like.

33:29.890 --> 33:32.020
As long as I have this power...

33:59.710 --> 34:00.750
Which way?

34:04.590 --> 34:05.990
Jeff! Behind you!

34:26.450 --> 34:27.920
Jeff, do you want my shotgun?

34:28.160 --> 34:29.240
That shotgun's...

34:39.250 --> 34:40.260
Jeff!

34:48.010 --> 34:49.460
Damn you!

34:49.930 --> 34:51.810
You bastard!

34:56.730 --> 34:57.270
Are you okay?

34:58.650 --> 34:59.480
What?

34:59.490 --> 35:00.490
Don't worry about me.

35:00.530 --> 35:01.990
Go on ahead.

35:02.110 --> 35:03.950
I'll slow 'em down.

35:06.860 --> 35:09.150
See ya. Let's meet at the bar.

35:10.900 --> 35:11.860
Understood.

35:44.430 --> 35:44.760
Ryu!

35:45.050 --> 35:45.640
Irene!

35:46.020 --> 35:46.770
Why are you here?

35:47.030 --> 35:48.950
Be careful, he's got a gun.

35:49.420 --> 35:51.940
At last you're here, Dragon Ninja.

35:52.360 --> 35:53.690
You bastard...

35:54.170 --> 35:54.900
That's...

35:54.990 --> 35:56.720
You know it already, don't you?

35:57.140 --> 35:59.710
The power of the Dark Gods that I have created.

36:00.020 --> 36:01.030
Created?

36:01.270 --> 36:01.990
Impossible.

36:02.310 --> 36:07.400
When you fought Jaquio, I recorded the
 surge of power from the Dark Gods.

36:07.430 --> 36:09.370
I made this based off that.

36:09.370 --> 36:13.790
Along with the Superhuman Manufacturing
Device that you destroyed.

36:16.710 --> 36:18.930
Do you not care if Miss Lu dies?

36:21.940 --> 36:22.760
Robert!

36:23.460 --> 36:25.550
Oh my, oh my, even you're here...

36:25.600 --> 36:33.160
If they let a normal human through, I need to alter
 their programming to make them better fighters.

36:33.240 --> 36:36.260
You bastard, making all those weird things...

36:36.280 --> 36:37.900
Stop, there's a girl here.

36:42.030 --> 36:44.070
You've done well, Ned.

36:44.090 --> 36:46.040
This ends your usefulness.

36:46.320 --> 36:48.160
Professor Bucky-Wise!

36:50.790 --> 36:51.750
Ryu!

36:54.840 --> 36:55.710
Are you okay?

36:57.420 --> 36:59.300
Now then, Dragon Ninja.

36:59.300 --> 37:03.340
Shall you settle things... with
your old, old acquaintance?

37:03.370 --> 37:04.760
I don't know who you are!

37:07.720 --> 37:11.230
Can you see the form of the Evil God inside me?

37:11.230 --> 37:12.430
What?

37:12.520 --> 37:15.810
I was the one who recorded the
surge of the Evil God's power.

37:15.810 --> 37:18.110
And I had Ned make it based off that.

37:19.570 --> 37:21.280
He's no fool.

37:21.360 --> 37:25.450
When he knew how wonderful this power was, he was overjoyed and agreed to cooperate with me.

37:25.530 --> 37:31.420
Well, at first, I kidnapped his
daughter and forced him to.

37:31.440 --> 37:33.870
Then it was his daughter who called for me?

37:40.380 --> 37:42.550
She's our precious daughter.

37:42.910 --> 37:44.090
Katherine...

37:58.090 --> 37:59.610
Katherine, come here!

38:03.010 --> 38:04.010
Let her go.

38:09.270 --> 38:12.840
He thought he was finished because
he had the power of the Evil God,

38:12.840 --> 38:15.840
but this, in the end, is just a replica.

38:15.840 --> 38:20.440
To break the seal, there is one
more thing that is needed.

38:24.740 --> 38:25.570
It can't be...

38:26.160 --> 38:27.190
The Evil God's...

38:28.030 --> 38:31.130
Yes. Part of the Evil God's body...

38:31.150 --> 38:35.670
When the Dragon Ninja sealed the Evil
God, those who longed for his return

38:36.130 --> 38:38.790
cut his body into pieces and split
it up among themselves.

38:39.050 --> 38:41.340
But with this alone, nothing can be done.

38:41.350 --> 38:44.470
The Evils God's body and the Evil God's power...

38:44.470 --> 38:47.140
These two are the keys that will
break the seal of the Evil God.

38:49.640 --> 38:54.020
All that's left then is to settle things
with my old, old acquaintance...

38:54.020 --> 38:55.750
Though I know how it will end.

38:56.560 --> 38:58.900
I don't care about my duty as a Dragon Ninja.

38:59.360 --> 39:01.860
All that matters to me is Irene!

39:02.570 --> 39:03.190
Ryu...

39:05.610 --> 39:09.670
Melodrama without considering the
circumstances is mere comedy!

39:09.730 --> 39:15.230
As long as you're here, as long as this evil power
 exists... then Irene and I will never be anything.

39:15.770 --> 39:17.370
So I'm going to defeat you!

39:19.760 --> 39:23.310
No matter what you do, the seal will be broken.

40:13.540 --> 40:15.180
Hide somewhere!

40:15.190 --> 40:16.570
No, I'm going too!

40:25.060 --> 40:26.430
Stay here.

40:33.020 --> 40:33.810
Dammit...

40:33.820 --> 40:36.070
Stop moving! Stop moving!

40:45.090 --> 40:45.720
Ryu!

41:12.080 --> 41:13.440
What an asshole...

41:14.120 --> 41:15.760
Hey, Irene!

41:29.970 --> 41:30.670
Irene!

41:33.640 --> 41:34.260
Irene...

41:39.180 --> 41:39.980
Irene....

42:01.710 --> 42:02.440
Ryu!

42:18.600 --> 42:19.600
Ryu!

42:36.770 --> 42:37.640
Ryu!

42:45.780 --> 42:46.900
Ryu!

43:27.720 --> 43:28.550
Irene...

43:43.280 --> 43:44.540
Ryu!

44:12.670 --> 44:15.470
Sara, you don't need to be that mad.

44:15.480 --> 44:17.150
Hey, Sara!

44:17.150 --> 44:18.980
Let's go get a drink!

44:21.030 --> 44:21.950
Sara–!

44:24.570 --> 44:26.740
I told you to take me too!

44:28.260 --> 44:29.080
Sara...

44:29.370 --> 44:30.700
I'm alive!

44:31.450 --> 44:33.370
Let's get married! Married!

44:33.540 --> 44:35.210
H-Hey, Robert!

44:35.230 --> 44:37.170
Think about where we are!

44:37.500 --> 44:39.390
Let's head straight to a church.

44:40.090 --> 44:41.670
Say cheese, Sara!

44:42.420 --> 44:44.510
Hey, don't take my picture!

44:45.090 --> 44:47.170
It's the memento of a lifetime!

45:10.590 --> 45:16.630
<i>Mayonaka ni hitori kiku FM no
Listening to the FM radio all alone in the middle of the night</i>

45:17.270 --> 45:23.400
<i>Saigo no baraado kiete yuku
The final ballad fades out</i>

45:24.210 --> 45:30.210
<i>Anata e no daiyaru o tsuzukete mo
I keep on dialing you on the phone</i>

45:31.150 --> 45:37.090
<i>Kurikaesu beru no oto dake
but all I hear is the sound of repeating bells</i>

45:38.190 --> 45:44.130
<i>Call me again konna ni kimochi de
Call me again, with these same feelings</i>

45:44.130 --> 45:51.470
<i>Anata o shibaritaku wa nai kedo
Although I don't want to tie you up</i>

45:51.830 --> 45:57.870
<i>Call me again koe ga kikitai
Call me again, I want to hear your voice</i>

45:57.870 --> 46:05.510
<i>Furueru kono omoi o shizumete
Calm these trembling emotions</i>

46:32.870 --> 46:39.950
<i>Furimukeba toki no umi ni hikaru yume
When looking over your shoulder, the sea sparkles with dreams</i>

46:39.950 --> 46:46.690
<i>Ima mo kono mune kogashiteru
Even now, my chest is burning</i>

46:46.690 --> 46:53.560
<i>Kaze no naka itsumo tooku mitsumeteta
Always staring far into the wind</i>

46:53.560 --> 47:00.670
<i>Sonna anata ga mabushikute
That's how dazzling you are</i>

47:01.970 --> 47:08.180
<i>Arubamu no peeji kara maiochita
Our smiles from the photos that day</i>

47:08.810 --> 47:15.450
<i>Ano hi no shashin no hohoemi
fluttered down from the pages of my album</i>

47:15.750 --> 47:21.790
<i>Omoide wa kaeranai atsui suna
Those memories are gone, now a hot sand</i>

47:22.660 --> 47:29.260
<i>Yubi kara koborete yuku dake
It's just fallen out of my fingers</i>

47:29.630 --> 47:35.500
<i>Call me again nani mo iranai
Call me again, I don't need anything else</i>

47:35.540 --> 47:43.110
<i>Anata wa jiyuu no mama sono mama
 As free as you are, just like that</i>

47:43.240 --> 47:49.120
<i>Call me again dakedo konya wa
Call me again, but just for tonight</i>

47:49.280 --> 47:57.530
<i>Mou ichido anata no koe kikasete
Let me hear your voice once more</i>

